#
# Disable WiFi power saving on wlan interfaces (e.g. Orange Pi 5B AP6275P /
# BCM43752 over PCIe). brcmfmac defaults power_save ON, which makes the radio
# sleep and miss association/beacon frames -> WiFi shows "enabled" but only
# connects after repeated retries / toggling off and on, especially on 5 GHz.
# Forcing power_save off at interface creation makes association immediate and
# reliable. ROCKNIX RK3588 uses NetworkManager + iwd with no dispatcher.d and a
# read-only rootfs, so a udev rule is the reliable place for this.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="wlan*", RUN+="/usr/sbin/iw dev $name set power_save off"
